  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> be the centres of the two circles where the poles of height <math><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>b</mi></math> respectively stand making angles <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>30</mn></mrow> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>60</mn></mrow> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math> respectively at the point <math><mi>O</mi></math> where these circles touch each other externally.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/43fed9d2-f45b-4e29-8ae9-153045135cda.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.16667in;height:1.61319in\" /><br />Sum of the radii of the two circles<br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>cot</mi><msup> <mrow> <mn>30</mn></mrow> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> <mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>cot</mi><msup> <mrow> <mn>60</mn></mrow> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo></math> distance between the centres of the two circles.",
